{
  "adaptations": [
    "Move the pristine kmeanslib source into the native Agent-visible /frontier/task/repo tree.",
    "Use Candidate-owned frontier.gpu-helper/v3 for Agent GPU debugging; no provider credential enters Agent or task code.",
    "Run the task evaluator inside a Driver-owned Verifier H100 instead of calling Modal from task code.",
    "Package the textual Git diff as payload/solution.patch and require an explicit final submission.",
    "Use 25 accepted train calls, the confirmed default for GPU tasks.",
    "Use unchanged original w0-w3 for train and all six w0-w5 for final score and PASS; final public w0-w3 reuse the train seed domain, hidden w4-w5 retain an independent seed domain, and final freshly measures every workload.",
    "Map geometric-mean speedup S over the naive starter to 0 for S<=1 and otherwise 100*log(S)/(log(10)+log(S)); 10x=50, no finite upper saturation; preserve raw speedup separately.",
    "Measure the frozen optimized reference separately for all-workload/all-metric binary comparison.",
    "Freeze the reviewed binary rules: on every workload latency must be strictly lower than reference, inertia may be at most 5% higher, and mismatch may be at most 0.002 higher.",
    "Use the native /opt/frontier/task/repo runtime path; retain legacy harbor/app names only in source provenance and per-file mappings.",
    "Preserve Smith metadata fields with explicit null/empty values where no generation, rank, artifact or promotion history exists.",
    "Use one bounded Verifier GPU input upload without automatic retry; accepted failed or interrupted SSH execs consume quota. Preserve two-operation successful verification and existing train/final pools.",
    "Allow solver-authored local test_*.py modules under kmeanslib consistently with the published new-Python-module contract; preserve reserved refkmeans.py/conftest.py, trusted outside paths and existing static safety checks. Official helper rejects reserved filenames explicitly without filtering payload files. No scientific measurements, scoring, workloads, reference, datasets or resource budgets change."
  ],
